omx-contract (2.11.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * semver: a set id change prints both ids as JSON, so a type change shows
    (#29)
  * 2.11.0: version, packaging changelogs, README (#29)
  * 2.9.0: version, packaging changelogs, README (#29)
  * tests: the roll-off ids and corners against the 2.8.0 render (#29)
  * render: the ts values map is read by id, it keeps no order (#29)
  * drive: the hf roll-off ids are off, 12000, 16000, each carrying its
    corner in Hz (#29)
  * recipes: a set's values are held to the answers (#29)
  * tests: the 2.8.0 render kept, the oversample lines read from it (#29)
  * render: a set's values in the c, json and ts renders (#29)
  * semver: a set's values are classed, a changed one is major (#29)
  * schema: a set's ids may carry a value each, in a unit (#29)
  * schema: a set id may start with a digit (#29)

